Atlas overlay patch 0010: build/atlas-anchors
Why: the hook lines every Atlas area would otherwise add to the same engine files, added once so
14 patch authors never edit the same file: the string parts chrome/app/atlas/<area>_strings.grdp in
the root grd, the build targets of chrome/browser/ui/atlas and components/atlas_{host,pages}, the
pak and resource ids of the Atlas pages, one call of atlas::RegisterProfilePrefs() (each area
registers its own prefs there), one dependency for the unit tests of every area, and the hosts of
the new tab and first-run pages. The new files themselves are the overlay tree (atlas/tree.list),
not part of this patch. No lower tier reaches build files.
Files: chrome/app/generated_resources.grd, chrome/browser/BUILD.gn, chrome/browser/ui/BUILD.gn,
 chrome/chrome_paks.gni, tools/gritsettings/resource_ids.spec, chrome/common/webui_url_constants.h,
 chrome/browser/prefs/browser_prefs.cc, chrome/test/BUILD.gn, chrome/app/generated_resources.grd.gritdeps
Test filter: compile of a dev slot with the empty areas; atlas/tests/test_series.sh
Rebase risk: M (nine files, all lists that move often; hunks are new blocks between engine lines,
 the resource_ids one sits under the inherited onboarding entry)
Release: 0.13
License: GPL-3.0-or-later (hunks in files the inherited series patches)
Verified at: 156.0.8078.79, prepared tree with the inherited and platform series applied

